# Scarcity Isle (the moddyisle level jar, #2750) on the PUBLIC core: a new player arrives and gets his own island.
# tools/play.sh passes the Isle's properties (world id, rules file, island spacing), exactly what a server's launcher sets.
@intent a new player on Scarcity Isle is welcomed and stands on his own island in the sky
@world flat seed=1

@step he joins
# the Isle's first-join words (worlds/isle.json "intro", in the level jar; the core reads it through manifestText)
@expect chat Welcome to Scarcity Isle within 90s

@step his island
# the island is built a few ticks after the claim, then he is moved onto it: up at Y 63 (the flat world is at -60)
@wait 5s
@repeat 30 until execute if entity @s[y=60,dy=12]
@wait 1s
@end-repeat
@assert execute if entity @s[y=60,dy=12]
# on the island's grass, 120 blocks above the flat world's
@assert execute at @s if block ~ ~-1 ~ minecraft:grass_block
@shot his-island
